{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentOrbitInvariants"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_diagram_equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.monodromyN_diagram_equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance.lean#L90-L104","doc":"**Monodromy is diagram-equivariant**: the `q = i` Jordan nilpotent\nat the image generator pulls back along a diagram symmetry to the\nnilpotent at the source generator. Conjugation edges are NOT covered —\ninner automorphisms need not preserve length; that case is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_length","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance.lean#L72-L88","doc":"**Diagram symmetries preserve Coxeter length.** One direction maps\na reduced word; the other applies the inverse symmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_symm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_symm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance.lean#L58-L70","doc":"The inverse symmetry undoes `diagramHom`, pointwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_wordProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_wordProd","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentMonodromyEquivariance.lean#L47-L56","doc":"A diagram symmetry maps word products to word products of the\nmapped word. ","signatureChunk":0}]}